module

public import Theory.SpecificGroups.C4SquareSignSwapCentricData
public import Theory.GroupTheory.SubgroupEnumeration

/-!
# Generating words for the centric candidates

Each coordinate carrier is generated by at most four specified elements.
A table of positive words supplies a normal form for every member; the
identities in the model are checked by Lean's kernel. These give the exact
closure description used by subgroup enumeration and a small set on which
to compare homomorphisms. The finite table is only witness data.

Source: direct calculations in the sign-and-swap model for Stellmacher
(8.6)(a), `refs/latex/stellmacher-n-group.tex`.
-/

namespace C4SquareSignSwap
open Theory.GroupTheory

